        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Included a video showing the issue. The buffer count is in the bottom left corner in the statusline. https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/883d2bc4-4625-4351-ad47-10df2bbf0545\n\nThere is no notification that session is read on the second Neovim opening. At the end of the first and at the start of the third instances the counter in the left shows `11|0`  and there is a notification that session is read. So I conclude that the local session wasn't read for some reason during the second opening and it **needs** to be read first in order to be autowritten before Neovim closes. You can verify which session is currently loaded (if any) with `:=vim.v.this_session`: it should show path to the session file if loaded or nothing if there is no current session.\n\nI'd also note that autoreading from 'mini.sessions' itself is not done if there is a dashboard file opened during startup. So make sure to properly call `MiniSessions.read()` to ensure that session is read (using no arguments will first [try loading local session](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b612a069d1fe99300da43629e0e9c7a1a9b0acda/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L133-L135) which should be ok for this use case).\n\nClosing as this is most certainly not an issue with 'mini.sessions'.",
